# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
# `/node_modules` is anchored to the repo root, so a nested one is NOT covered:
# voice-gateway/node_modules appeared (vite cache) and was untracked-but-unignored,
# one broad `git add -A` away from committing a dependency tree.
/node_modules
voice-gateway/node_modules/
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# local Claude preview/dev config
.claude/
__pycache__/
*.log
wake-diag.log

# ── Personal Config: real profile data stays LOCAL ───────────────────────────
# "Private repo" is not the same as "not exposed": history is permanent, a push
# or a shared branch leaks it, and a later .gitignore does not undo a commit.
# Tracked: schema, loader, synthetic *.example.yaml. Never: Roei's own data.
voice-gateway/profiles/*.yaml
!voice-gateway/profiles/*.example.yaml

# ── Knowledge-extraction raw artifacts: LOCAL BACKUP, never tracked ──────────
# The harvest/journal payloads quote source material verbatim — political,
# family-loyalty, dating and biographical excerpts — and carry ~284 absolute
# local paths. The synthesis neutralises that content; the raw layer does not.
# A local backup and a git history are different needs: this survives the loss
# of ~/cluod code (which has no remote) without entering permanent history.
# Tracked instead: the consolidated report and a sanitized manifest.
#
# `raw/*` not `raw/` — git never descends into an excluded DIRECTORY, so the
# .gitkeep negation below would be dead with the directory form.
docs/knowledge-inventory/raw/*
!docs/knowledge-inventory/raw/.gitkeep

# ── Knowledge System: its own PRIVATE repo, nested here ──────────────────────
# knowledge-system/ is a separate git repository with a private remote. It is
# excluded here in full, not partially: `entries/` and `candidates/` are the
# source documents from which person.yaml and music.yaml are derived, so they
# are strictly MORE sensitive than the profile data line 57 already withholds —
# and THIS repo is public (github.com/roeik18-dotcom/-nexus-globe).
#
# Excluding it is what gives the corpus real version control: history, review
# and recovery all live in the private repo, where entries/ IS tracked. The
# alternative was tracking it here, which publishes it.
#
# This line must exist BEFORE `git init` runs inside the directory — otherwise
# one `git add -A` adds the files or a gitlink before the guard is in place.
knowledge-system/

# ── Philos event log: runtime state, not repo content ────────────────────────
# `.philos-data/philos-events.jsonl` holds what users have actually done on THIS
# machine. The seeded history is code (`valueGroupLog.ts`) and stays reviewable;
# what a run records is not a source artefact, and committing it would make one
# laptop's session everybody's starting state.
.philos-data/

# ── Merlin storage roots: machine-local paths, never tracked ─────────────────
# storage_root -> absolute base is a fact about ONE laptop. The example is
# committed so the shape is discoverable; the real map is not.
voice-gateway/config/storage_roots.yaml
voice-gateway/config/storage_roots.json

# PHILOS/HUMAN source corpus manifest — contains real absolute local paths
# and filenames (some personal/sensitive), same discipline as
# docs/knowledge-inventory/raw/. See source-corpus/README.md.
source-corpus/MANIFEST.json
source-corpus/philos/**
source-corpus/human/**
source-corpus/archive/**
!source-corpus/philos/.gitkeep
!source-corpus/human/.gitkeep
!source-corpus/archive/.gitkeep

# ── PHILOS canon runtime records: real personal data, never tracked ──────────
# The same class as `.philos-data/` above, and simply missed when that rule was
# written. These files hold person_roei's REAL Observations, Needs, Offers,
# Actions, Effects and identity links — verbatim Hebrew self-reports about his
# own emotional state and community commitments. THIS REPO IS PUBLIC
# (github.com/roeik18-dotcom/-nexus-globe), and history is permanent: a single
# `git add -A` would publish them irreversibly.
#
# Directory-scoped deliberately: everything under here is written by a run, and
# no source artefact lives in it.
.philos-canon-data/

# ── Merlin runtime state and voice transcripts: personal, never tracked ──────
# `dashboard/events.jsonl` carries a `transcript_excerpt` field — literal
# transcripts of what was said out loud to the assistant. `state/*.json` holds
# the real generated day-opening briefing and an 836 KB bookmark snapshot.
#
# FILE-scoped, not directory-scoped, and that distinction is load-bearing:
# `voice-gateway/state/` also contains `.py` modules. Ignoring the directory
# would silently exclude source code, which is exactly the mistake this pass
# was asked to avoid.
voice-gateway/dashboard/events.jsonl
voice-gateway/state/*.json

# ── project_knowledge: the CODE stays trackable, the generated index does not ─
# This directory is 12 real Python modules (api, chunker, indexer, retrieval,
# store, discovery, …) plus three generated artefacts. Only the artefacts are
# excluded — `index.db` is a 17.8 MB search index built over local content, and
# both `knowledge_query.log` and `stats.json` record real user queries verbatim,
# together with absolute local home-directory paths. (Those queries are
# deliberately NOT quoted as examples here — this file is bound for a public
# repo, and an illustration of the leak would be the leak.)
#
# Again file-scoped on purpose: `voice-gateway/project_knowledge/` must NOT be
# ignored as a directory.
voice-gateway/project_knowledge/index.db
voice-gateway/project_knowledge/knowledge_query.log
voice-gateway/project_knowledge/stats.json

# ── corpus/: the scaffolding READMEs are tracked, future contents are not ─────
# The four README.md files are category definitions and contain no personal
# data, so they stay trackable. Everything else is excluded IN ADVANCE, because
# the directory's own stated purpose is "כל מידע שהוא ייחודי לרועי" (all
# information unique to Roei) — a `.gitignore` written after the first commit
# does not undo it.
#
# `corpus/*/*` (not `corpus/**`) so the subdirectories themselves stay
# un-excluded and the README negation below can actually take effect — git
# cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
corpus/*/*
!corpus/*/README.md

# ── Editor/script .bak snapshots: redundant copies, not history ──────────────
# 22 of these accumulated during the Merlin work. 15 are backups of files that
# ARE tracked in git, so real history already covers them and a second copy on
# disk is noise. Ignored here rather than deleted — the files stay on disk.
#
# BOTH separators are covered on purpose: 9 use `.bak-<label>` and 6 use
# `.bak.<label>`. A `*.bak-*`-only rule would have missed the six dot-form
# backups of merlin_service.py and wake_trigger.py.
*.bak-*
*.bak.*

# The seven exceptions below are NOT redundant: their live counterpart is
# itself untracked, or (for the launchd plist) no longer exists at all — this
# .bak is the ONLY surviving copy. They are negated back in so COMMIT_2 can
# preserve them. Full paths, because the suffixes collide with the redundant
# set (`.bak-master-20260808-215137` is redundant for context_builder.py but
# unique for domain_router.py).
!voice-gateway/launch/com.merlin.voice.plist.bak-preapp-20260814
!voice-gateway/app/domain_router.py.bak-master-20260808-215137
!voice-gateway/orientation/domains.py.bak-20260808-213651
!voice-gateway/service/barge_detector.py.bak-bargetiming-20260808-165144
!voice-gateway/service/control_panel.html.bak-console-20260810-230950
!voice-gateway/service/control_panel.html.bak-precolor
!voice-gateway/service/control_panel.py.bak-console-20260810-230950

# ── Merlin relationship memory: personal runtime state, never tracked ────────
# 817 accumulated memories about the user — preferences, habits, events, and 25
# memories about other PEOPLE. Runtime state written by the assistant, not
# source. It was tracked and reached a remote branch before this rule existed;
# `git rm --cached` (same commit) stops it going further. The local file stays
# on disk, untouched.
#
# Directory-scoped, and deliberately NOT `memory/`: the memory CODE lives at
# voice-gateway/app/memory/ and must stay trackable. Only the data store here
# is excluded.
voice-gateway/memory/relationship/
